// tools/ucd/flat_baseline.fi -- THE BASELINE OF THE MEASUREMENT, kept.
//
// This was `lib/js/unicode_id.fi` until round 95: the ID_Start and
// ID_Continue ranges of ECMA-262 12.7.1, GENERATED BY A PYTHON SCRIPT
// (tools/js/gen_unicode_id.py) out of the `unicodedata` module of whatever
// Python happened to run it -- Unicode version 14.0.0. 647 + 754 ranges,
// pushed into a `mem.CpBuf` at start up and searched with a binary search.
//
// The JavaScript lexer no longer uses it; it asks
// `generated/unicode_tables.fi` (Unicode 17.0.0, built out of the UCD by
// `bash tools/ucd/build.sh`). The file stays here because
// `tools/ucd/bench_tables.fi` measures the new table AGAINST it -- a
// comparison whose other side has been deleted is not a comparison.
//
// Unicode version of the generator: 14.0.0
// ID_Start ranges: 647, ID_Continue ranges: 754
